Lineage guarantees

    Every artifact must include lineage linking to zero or more parents

    Lineage is transitive and queryable via GET /v1/lineage/{artifact_id}

    Lineage queries return DAG with depth limit parameter to avoid runaway traversal

Idempotency

    X-Request-Id ensures duplicate client retries do not create duplicate artifacts or jobs

    Server stores request id → response mapping for a configurable TTL (e.g., 24 hours)

Error Model and Status Codes

HTTP status mapping

    200 OK — successful GET

    201 Created — synchronous create success

    202 Accepted — async job accepted

    400 Bad Request — validation error; response includes error_code and details

    401 Unauthorized — missing/invalid token

    403 Forbidden — permission denied

    404 Not Found — artifact/job not found

    409 Conflict — idempotency conflict or license conflict

